Local Object Storage Exposure Simulator
Prerequisites
Basic Linux command line knowledge
Understanding of file permissions
Familiarity with web browsers
No prior cloud storage experience required
Learning Objectives
By completing this lab, you will:

Understand how misconfigured object storage can expose sensitive data
Learn to simulate a local object storage service
Identify public access vulnerabilities
Practice detecting and verifying storage exposure risks
Environment Setup
Al Nafi provides a bare-metal Linux machine. You'll install all required tools during this lab.

Tools We'll Install:
MinIO: Open-source object storage server (S3-compatible)
MinIO Client (mc): Command-line tool for managing storage
curl: For testing HTTP access
Task 1: Install and Configure MinIO Object Storage
