Key Takeaways:
Misconfigured storage is a critical security risk: Public access to sensitive data can lead to data breaches
Default settings matter: Always verify access policies before storing data
Detection is essential: Regular scanning helps identify misconfigurations
Principle of least privilege: Only grant necessary access permissions
Real-World Significance:
Object storage misconfigurations are among the most common cloud security issues, leading to major data breaches. Understanding how to identify and prevent these exposures is crucial for cybersecurity professionals. This lab simulates real-world scenarios where sensitive data becomes publicly accessible due to incorrect permissions.

